      "body": "  ## Overview\r\n  Skip the RTLD_GLOBAL promotion of libtorch_cpu.so when HSA_TOOLS_LIB is\r\n  set, indicating an external HSA profiling tool (e.g. rocm-trace-lite) is\r\n  active.  The RTLD_GLOBAL promotion and external HSA tools are mutually\r\n  exclusive — only one can be active at a time.  When HSA_TOOLS_LIB is not\r\n  set, behavior is unchanged.\r\n\r\n  ## Root cause\r\n  PR #56190 added `_maybe_promote_torch_symbols_for_rocm()` which loads\r\n  libtorch_cpu.so with RTLD_GLOBAL before `import torch` to enable\r\n  torch.profiler GPU tracing on ROCm.  This unconditionally pulls\r\n  libhsa-runtime64 into the global symbol scope, which breaks external\r\n  HSA profiling tools that were previously working.  The\r\n  rocprofiler_configure symbol exported by libtorch_cpu.so and the\r\n  HSA_TOOLS_LIB OnLoad callback both try to register with\r\n  libhsa-runtime64 for queue interception; when libtorch_cpu.so is loaded\r\n  RTLD_GLOBAL first, it shadows the external tool's registration and\r\n  prevents its OnLoad callback from firing — resulting in zero GPU kernel\r\n  records captured.\r\n\r\n  ## Changes\r\n  - Added an early return in `_maybe_promote_torch_symbols_for_rocm()`\r\n    when `HSA_TOOLS_LIB` is set, skipping the RTLD_GLOBAL promotion so\r\n    the external tool's intercept path works correctly.\r\n  - Added docstring explaining the mutual exclusivity and why the skip is\r\n    necessary.\r\n\r\n  ## Tests\r\n  - Verified default behavior (HSA_TOOLS_LIB unset): libtorch_cpu.so is\r\n    promoted with RTLD_GLOBAL as before, torch.profiler GPU tracing\r\n    works correctly.\r\n  - Verified with HSA_TOOLS_LIB set: RTLD_GLOBAL promotion is skipped,\r\n    external HSA profiling tool's OnLoad callback fires successfully and\r\n    GPU kernel records are captured.",
